  "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061(-\\frac{3}{7})=2.013\\,707\u2026\u22482.0137\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $2.0137$ lies inside the specified domain, our first solution, rounded to one decimal place, is $x=2.0.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the second quadrant and has a reference angle of \n\n$$\n{\\theta }_{R}=\\pi -2.0137\u22481.1279.\n$$\n\nSince $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=1.1279.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952163/assets/157096afa9d3de44710dfa11c99f1f699815156fbcd5d649c1b4048dbbba9913.png)\n\nSince the second solution $x$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +1.1279 \\\\  & \u22484.3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, arranged in ascending order, the solutions are $x=2.0$ and $x=4.3.$",
